ich of the following are second-order ordinary differential equations?\n\nI. - $9x{y}^{''}+8{y}^{'}=4$\nII. - $\\sqrt{{y}^{''}+x}=3y$\nIII. - ${y}^{‴}+{x}^{2}{y}^{''}=3$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is of second-order if the largest derivative term in the equation is ${y}^{''}.$\n\nKeeping this in mind, let's check each given equation.\n\n- Equation I is a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{''}.$\n\n- Equation II is also a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{''}.$\n\n- Equation III is not a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{‴},$ so this is a third-order differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] ["Identifying the Order of an Ordinary Differential Equation" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234489 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "443c0bd0-2e77-50a8-91d3-a288d4ee852b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Order of an Ordinary Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11ad9833-c6bb-53f7-a6ff-f776f82ce01a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357903} {:answer/id #uuid "13b7f10e-fcc6-55af-bcf8-f20b6af5714c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357920} {:answer/id #uuid "1dabb7fb-af72-545e-91aa-40401d07d443" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358008} {:answer/id #uuid "5aa2da80-b1e7-5953-8e7b-f40dca5848eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358538} {:answer/id #uuid "b943a100-b054-5e11-b08e-b46f1c2b0e26" :answer/type